# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Amplitude encoding {#amplitude-encoding}"
msgstr "Amplitude encoding {#amplitude-encoding}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Amplitude encoding encodes data into the amplitudes of a quantum state. It represents a normalized classical $N$-dimensional data vector, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}$, as the amplitudes of a $n$-qubit quantum state, $|\\psi_x\\rangle$:\n"
msgstr "Ang amplitude encoding ay nagko-encode ng data sa mga amplitude ng isang quantum state. Kinakatawan nito ang isang normalized na klasikal na $N$-dimensional na data vector, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}$, bilang mga amplitude ng isang $n$-qubit na quantum state, $|\\psi_x\\rangle$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{(j)}_x\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\alpha}\\sum_{i=1}^N x^{(j)}_i |i\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi^{(j)}_x\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\alpha}\\sum_{i=1}^N x^{(j)}_i |i\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $N$ is the same dimension of the data vectors as before, $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_i$ is the $i^{th}$ element of $\\vec{x}^{(j)}$ and $|i\\rangle$ is the $i^{th}$ computational basis state. Here, $\\alpha$ is a normalization constant to be determined from the data being encoded. This is the normalization condition imposed by quantum mechanics:\n"
msgstr "kung saan ang $N$ ay ang parehong dimensyon ng mga data vector tulad ng dati, ang $\\vec{x}^{(j)}_i$ ay ang $i^{th}$ na elemento ng $\\vec{x}^{(j)}$ at ang $|i\\rangle$ ay ang $i^{th}$ na computational basis state. Dito, ang $\\alpha$ ay isang normalization constant na matutukoy mula sa data na ine-encode. Ito ang normalization condition na ipinapataw ng quantum mechanics:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{i=1}^N \\left|x^{(j)}_i\\right|^2 = \\left|\\alpha\\right|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{i=1}^N \\left|x^{(j)}_i\\right|^2 = \\left|\\alpha\\right|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, this is a different condition than the min/max normalization used for each feature across all data vectors. Precisely how this is navigated will depend on your problem. But there is no way around the quantum mechanical normalization condition above.\n"
msgstr "Sa pangkalahatan, ito ay ibang kondisyon kaysa sa min/max normalization na ginagamit para sa bawat feature sa lahat ng data vector. Kung paano ito haharapin ay depende sa iyong problema. Ngunit walang paraan para maiwasan ang quantum mechanical normalization condition sa itaas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In amplitude encoding, each feature in a data vector is stored as an amplitude of a different quantum state. As a system of $n$ qubits provides $2^n$ amplitudes, amplitude encoding of $N$ features requires $n \\ge \\mathrm{log}_2(N)$ qubits.\n"
msgstr "Sa amplitude encoding, bawat feature sa isang data vector ay naka-imbak bilang amplitude ng ibang quantum state. Dahil ang isang sistema ng $n$ na qubit ay nagbibigay ng $2^n$ na amplitude, ang amplitude encoding ng $N$ na feature ay nangangailangan ng $n \\ge \\mathrm{log}_2(N)$ na qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As an example, let's encode the first vector in our example dataset $\\text{X}_\\text{ex}$, $\\vec{x}^{(1)} = (4,8,5)$ using amplitude encoding. Normalizing the resulting vector, we get:\n"
msgstr "Bilang halimbawa, i-encode natin ang unang vector sa ating halimbawang dataset $\\text{X}_\\text{ex}$, ang $\\vec{x}^{(1)} = (4,8,5)$ gamit ang amplitude encoding. Sa pag-normalize ng resultang vector, nakukuha natin:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{i=1}^N \\left|x^{(1)}_i\\right|^2 = 4^2+8^2+5^2 = 105 = \\left|\\alpha\\right|^2 \\rightarrow \\alpha = \\sqrt{105}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{i=1}^N \\left|x^{(1)}_i\\right|^2 = 4^2+8^2+5^2 = 105 = \\left|\\alpha\\right|^2 \\rightarrow \\alpha = \\sqrt{105}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and the resulting 2-qubit quantum state would be:\n"
msgstr "at ang resultang 2-qubit na quantum state ay magiging:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(\\vec{x}^{(1)})\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{105}}(4|00\\rangle+8|01\\rangle+5|10\\rangle+0|11\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(\\vec{x}^{(1)})\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{105}}(4|00\\rangle+8|01\\rangle+5|10\\rangle+0|11\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the example above, the number of features in the vector $N=3$, is not a power of 2. When $N$ is not a power of 2, we simply choose a value for the number of qubits $n$ such that $2^n\\geq N$ and pad the amplitude vector with uninformative constants (here, a zero).\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawa sa itaas, ang bilang ng mga feature sa vector $N=3$ ay hindi isang kapangyarihan ng 2. Kapag ang $N$ ay hindi isang kapangyarihan ng 2, pumipili lang tayo ng halaga para sa bilang ng mga qubit $n$ na may $2^n\\geq N$ at dino-dagdagan ang amplitude vector ng mga walang-impormasyon na konstante (dito, isang zero).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Like in basis encoding, once we calculate what state will encode our dataset, in Qiskit we can use the `initialize` function to prepare it:\n"
msgstr "Tulad ng sa basis encoding, kapag nakalkulan na natin kung anong estado ang mag-eencode ng ating dataset, sa Qiskit ay maaari nating gamitin ang function na `initialize` para ihanda ito:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/19810c6d-8d60-49ee-bd6f-6f6fbd5e7363-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/19810c6d-8d60-49ee-bd6f-6f6fbd5e7363-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An advantage of amplitude encoding is the aforementioned requirement of only $\\mathrm{log}_2(N)$ qubits to encode. However, subsequent algorithms must operate on the amplitudes of a quantum state, and methods to prepare and measure the quantum states tend not to be efficient.\n"
msgstr "Isang kalamangan ng amplitude encoding ay ang nabanggit na pangangailangan ng $\\mathrm{log}_2(N)$ na qubit lamang para mag-encode. Gayunpaman, ang mga kasunod na algorithm ay kailangang gumana sa mga amplitude ng isang quantum state, at ang mga pamamaraan para ihanda at sukatin ang mga quantum state ay karaniwang hindi mahusay.\n"

