# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding with built-in feature maps {#encoding-with-built-in-feature-maps}"
msgstr "Pag-encode gamit ang mga built-in na feature map {#encoding-with-built-in-feature-maps}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding at arbitrary points {#encoding-at-arbitrary-points}"
msgstr "Pag-encode sa mga arbitrary na punto {#encoding-at-arbitrary-points}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Angle encoding, phase encoding, and dense encoding prepared product states with a feature encoded on each qubit (or two features per qubit). This is different from basis encoding and amplitude encoding, in that those methods make use of entangled states. There is not a 1:1 correspondence between data feature and qubit. In amplitude encoding, for example, you might have one feature as the amplitude of the state $|01\\rangle$ and another feature as the amplitude for $|10\\rangle$. Generally, methods that encode in product states yield shallower circuits and can store 1 or 2 features on each qubit. Methods that use entanglement and associate a feature with a state rather than a qubit result in deeper circuits, and can store more features per qubit on average.\n"
msgstr "Ang angle encoding, phase encoding, at dense encoding ay naghahanda ng mga product state na may isang feature na naka-encode sa bawat qubit (o dalawang feature bawat qubit). Ito ay naiiba sa basis encoding at amplitude encoding, dahil ang mga pamamaraang iyon ay gumagamit ng mga entangled state. Walang 1:1 na ugnayan sa pagitan ng isang data feature at isang qubit. Sa amplitude encoding, halimbawa, maaaring may isang feature bilang amplitude ng state $|01\\rangle$ at isa pang feature bilang amplitude ng $|10\\rangle$. Sa pangkalahatan, ang mga pamamaraang nag-e-encode sa product states ay nagbubunga ng mas mababaw na circuits at kayang mag-imbak ng 1 o 2 na feature sa bawat qubit. Ang mga pamamaraang gumagamit ng entanglement at nag-uugnay ng isang feature sa isang state sa halip na sa isang qubit ay nagbubunga ng mas malalim na circuits, at kayang mag-imbak ng mas maraming feature bawat qubit sa karaniwan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "But encoding need not be entirely in product states or entirely in entangled states as in amplitude encoding. Indeed, many encoding schemes built into Qiskit allow encoding both before and after an entanglement layer, as opposed to just at the beginning. This is known as \"data reuploading\". For related work, see references [5] and  [6].\n"
msgstr "Ngunit hindi kailangang maging ganap na nasa product states o ganap na nasa entangled states ang encoding tulad ng sa amplitude encoding. Sa katunayan, maraming encoding scheme na built-in sa Qiskit ang nagpapahintulot ng encoding bago at pagkatapos ng isang entanglement layer, kumpara sa pag-encode lamang sa simula. Ito ay tinatawag na \"data reuploading\". Para sa kaugnay na pananaliksik, tingnan ang mga sanggunian [5] at [6].\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this section, we will use and visualize a few of the built-in encoding schemes. All the methods in this section encode $N$ features as rotations on $N$ parameterized gates on $n$ qubits, where $n \\leq N$. Note that maximizing data loading for a given number of qubits is not the only consideration. In many cases, circuit depth may be an even more important consideration than qubit count.\n"
msgstr "Sa seksyong ito, gagamitin at ivi-visualize natin ang ilang built-in na encoding scheme. Lahat ng pamamaraan sa seksyong ito ay nag-e-encode ng $N$ na feature bilang mga rotasyon sa $N$ na parameterized gate sa $n$ qubit, kung saan $n \\leq N$. Tandaan na ang pag-maximize ng data loading para sa isang tiyak na bilang ng qubit ay hindi lang ang dapat isaalang-alang. Sa maraming kaso, ang lalim ng circuit ay maaaring mas mahalaga pa kaysa sa bilang ng qubit.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Efficient SU2 {#efficient-su2}"
msgstr "Efficient SU2 {#efficient-su2}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A common and useful example of encoding with entanglement is Qiskit's [`efficient_su2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.EfficientSU2) circuit. Impressively, this circuit can, for example, encode 8 features on only 2 qubits. Let's see this, and then try to understand how it is possible.\n"
msgstr "Isang karaniwang at kapaki-pakinabang na halimbawa ng pag-encode na may entanglement ay ang [`efficient_su2`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.EfficientSU2) circuit ng Qiskit. Kahanga-hanga, ang circuit na ito ay kayang, halimbawa, mag-encode ng 8 na feature sa 2 qubit lamang. Tignan natin ito, at pagkatapos ay subukang unawain kung paano ito posible.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/6b657226-ae95-41f6-b78b-5def930d0080-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-machine-learning/data-encoding/extracted-outputs/6b657226-ae95-41f6-b78b-5def930d0080-0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we write our state, we will use the Qiskit convention that least-significant qubits are ordered to the far right, as in $|q_2,q_1,q_0\\rangle$ or $|q_2\\rangle\\otimes|q_1\\rangle\\otimes|q_0\\rangle.$ These states can become very complicated very quickly, and this rare example may help explain why such states are seldom written out explicitly.\n"
msgstr "Habang isinusulat natin ang ating state, gagamitin natin ang Qiskit convention na ang mga least-significant qubit ay nakaayos sa pinakakanang bahagi, tulad ng sa $|q_2,q_1,q_0\\rangle$ o $|q_2\\rangle\\otimes|q_1\\rangle\\otimes|q_0\\rangle.$ Ang mga state na ito ay maaaring maging napakakumplikado agad, at ang bihirang halimbawang ito ay makakatulong na ipaliwanag kung bakit bihira nang isinusulat ang mga ganitong state nang tahasan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our system starts in the state $|00\\rangle.$ Up to the first barrier (a point we label $b1$), our states are:\n"
msgstr "Nagsisimula ang ating sistema sa state $|00\\rangle.$ Hanggang sa unang barrier (isang puntong tinutukoy natin bilang $b1$), ang ating mga state ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_{b1} = \\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}|1\\rangle\\right)\\otimes\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}|1\\rangle\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_{b1} = \\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}|1\\rangle\\right)\\otimes\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)|0\\rangle+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}|1\\rangle\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That's just dense encoding, which we've seen before. Now after the CNOT gate, at the second barrier ($b2$), our state is\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_{b2} = & \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)|00\\rangle+\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}|11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"+ & \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}|10\\rangle+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}e^{i\\theta_3}|01\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"We now apply the last set of single-qubit rotations and collect like states to obtain:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_{\\text{final}} = &\n"
"\\left[\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)\\right.\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay dense encoding lamang, na nakita na natin noon. Ngayon pagkatapos ng CNOT gate, sa ikalawang barrier ($b2$), ang ating state ay\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_{b2} = & \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)|00\\rangle+\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}|11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"+ & \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}|10\\rangle+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}e^{i\\theta_3}|01\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Ngayon ay ilalagay natin ang huling set ng mga single-qubit rotation at pagsamahin ang mga magkaparehong state upang makuha:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\begin{align*}\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle_{\\text{final}} = &\n"
"\\left[\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)\\right.\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"+ & \\left.\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}\\right]\n"
"|00\\rangle\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"+ & \\left.\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}\\right]\n"
"|00\\rangle\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '+ '
#, no-wrap
msgid "& \\left[\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)\\right.\\\\\n"
msgstr "& \\left[\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)-\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)\\right.\\\\\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"+ & \\left.\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(-\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}\\right]\n"
"e^{i\\theta_6}|01\\rangle\\\\\n"
msgstr ""
"+ & \\left.\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_0}{2}\\right)\\left(-\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\theta_1}{2}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_5}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_3}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta_4}{2}\\right)e^{i\\theta_2}\\right]\n"
"e^{i\\theta_6}|01\\rangle\\\\\n"

